**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A selection, a category or the whole of the user's library exports to a catalogue folder: one `.catalogue-json` manifest and one file per entry (001 §B 'Export: … a selection or a category → a catalogue folder'; 001 §A 'Catalogue folder layout': uniqueness per kind within a catalogue is checked on export; 001 §C '"Export my library" writes the user entries to a catalogue folder, which the recreated database imports'; the S3.3 brief). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`. (a) `CatalogueExportTarget = { folder : FolderName; name : CatalogueName }` is where a catalogue export goes and the name its manifest carries. (b) `LibraryExportError` (step 116) gains three cases, each documented and each with a `describe` line. `ExportCatalogueRefusedErr of CatalogueError`: the entries do not form a catalogue (`InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr` from `CatalogueData.tryCreate`), or the folder write failed. `ExportFolderHoldsCatalogueErr of reason : string`: the target folder already holds a catalogue manifest, naming the folder. `EmptyLibraryExportErr of reason : string`: there is nothing to export. (c) `CatalogueImportContext` gains `newCatalogueId : unit -> CatalogueId`, documented as the id an exported catalogue is minted under and injected as `newEntryId` is. (d) `member this.exportEntries (ids : LibraryEntryId list) (target : CatalogueExportTarget) : Result<CatalogueData, LibraryExportError>` works in this order, and nothing is pinned or written before its last two steps. (i) An empty list is `EmptyLibraryExportErr` naming the folder. (ii) Each distinct id's latest envelope is read through `tryLatestEnvelope` (`ExportedEntryNotHeldErr`, `ExportLibraryRefusedErr`). (iii) The user entries they reference join them. Every id in an exported content's `referencedEntryIds` (step 93) that is not yet exported, and for which `tryHeldEntry` answers a `UserManaged` entry, joins at its latest version, and its own references are followed the same way. A referenced built-in does not join, because every library imports the shipped catalogue. So a sample over Silicon exports alone, and an export of user entries never meets a built-in's file name. (iv) The per-kind name check comes first among the refusals: `CatalogueData.tryCreate (this.newCatalogueId ()) target.name VersionNumber.first envelopes` (step 32). Its refusal is `ExportCatalogueRefusedErr`, so two exported entries of one kind and one file name are refused, naming both (step 26's `DuplicateEntryFileNameErr`). (v) `(this.openCatalogue target.folder).readManifest ()` (steps 92, 98). `Ok manifest` or `CatalogueFileRejectedErr` is `ExportFolderHoldsCatalogueErr` naming the folder, so an export never overwrites a catalogue. Any other answer (no folder, no manifest) goes on; the writer creates a missing folder. (vi) Every envelope's version is pinned through `proxy.pinEntryVersion` (step 115). (vii) `writeCatalogue` writes the data (step 33: the entry files, then the manifest, each atomically; a folder holding an entry file the catalogue does not name is refused, and those pins stay, which only makes the next physics edit mint a version). The answer is the data written. (e) `member this.exportUserLibrary (target : CatalogueExportTarget) : Result<CatalogueData, LibraryExportError>` is `exportEntries` over every id `proxy.heldUserEntries ()` answers, inactive entries included, so a recreated library gets back everything the user owned (001 §C). A library holding no user entry is `EmptyLibraryExportErr`. A catalogue holds one version of each entry, its latest, because the folder names each entry's file by its name (001 §A). Each member doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.3. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`: `create`, its signature unchanged, fills `newCatalogueId` with a new GUID. `type CatalogueExportTarget with static member ofFolder (folder : FolderName) : CatalogueExportTarget` names the target by the folder's last segment (`Path.GetFileName` of the path without its trailing separator), so a chosen folder `…/Lab catalogue` exports as the catalogue `Lab catalogue`. The export dialogs call it (steps 119, 120). Its doc is one line. No merge into an existing catalogue, version bump of a re-export, progress report or option is added: each target folder becomes a new catalogue. (3) Tests. Each target is a fresh GUID folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "LibraryExportTests")`, not created beforehand. Entries are built with step 113's fixture and put through `putSealedEntries` after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`. `CatalogueImportContract` gains six facts, so each runs over both stores. `a catalogue export carries the user entries its entries reference, and importing it back reuses every entry`: `userCategoryContent` `Lab category`, `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass` with its `categoryOpt` set to that category, and `sampleContentOver` `Lab stack` over `Lab glass`. `exportEntries [ Lab stack ]` answers data whose envelopes are exactly those three, each equal to its held latest envelope. `CatalogueProxy.create` over the folder reads it back equal, its manifest named `target.name`. `proxy.decideCatalogue` of it answers three `SameContentHash` rows, each defaulting to `ReuseHeldEntry`, and `importCatalogue` of it MUST answer the same three reuse rows; explicit confirmation of their defaults MUST leave `heldUserEntries` unchanged. `a catalogue export pins every exported version`: after (E1)'s export, `Lab glass`, given the catalogue Langasite's complexity and saved through the set's `materials.saveMaterial`, resolves at versions 1 and 2, and `samples.removeSample` of `Lab stack` answers `SampleVersionPinnedErr`. `a catalogue export of two entries of one kind with one file name is refused, naming both, and pins and writes nothing`: two `userMaterialContent`s named `Lab glass` under two ids answer `ExportCatalogueRefusedErr (InvalidCatalogueEntriesErr (DuplicateEntryFileNameErr reason))`, whose reason names both entries (step 26). The target folder does not exist, and the first material, given Langasite's complexity and saved, still resolves at version 1 alone. `a catalogue export refuses a folder that already holds a catalogue`: after `Lab glass` is exported to the target, exporting `Lab stack` to it answers `ExportFolderHoldsCatalogueErr` naming the folder, and every file's text in it is unchanged. `Export my library writes every user entry, inactive ones included, and no built-in`: over `Lab category`, `Lab glass`, `Lab stack` and a `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` retired through `retireEntry`, `exportUserLibrary` answers data whose ids are exactly `heldUserEntries ()`'s four, none under `BuiltInProvenance`, and the folder reads back equal. `an export with nothing to write is refused`: `exportEntries []`, and `exportUserLibrary` over a library holding only the Built-in catalogue, each answer `EmptyLibraryExportErr`, and the target folder does not exist. `CatalogueImportSqliteTests` gains `a catalogue export pins the version row of every exported kind`: over a database the fact opens as the class's `freshImport` does, `Lab category`, `Lab glass`, `Lab stack` and a user source (the catalogue's first source under a fresh GUID id and `UserManaged`, built with `ofSourcePreset` under `UserProvenance`) are put. `exportEntries` of those four and of one built-in polarizer and one built-in detector leaves each exported version row `VersionPinned`, read through `run` and `tryStoredVersion`, while an unexported built-in source stays `VersionUnpinned`. `CatalogueFolderTests` gains `a catalogue export target is named by its folder`: `ofFolder (FolderName "D:/Exports/Lab catalogue")` and `ofFolder (FolderName "D:/Exports/Lab catalogue/")` each answer the folder as given and `CatalogueName "Lab catalogue"`. `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `every export error renders its condition and its payload` (step 116) covers the three new cases.

**Acceptance.** After catalogue export lands, `exportEntries` and `exportUserLibrary` MUST check per-kind file-name uniqueness before they pin, pin before they write, and never overwrite a catalogue folder; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a catalogue export carries the user entries its entries reference, and importing it back reuses every entry`, `a catalogue export pins every exported version`, `a catalogue export of two entries of one kind with one file name is refused, naming both, and pins and writes nothing`, `a catalogue export refuses a folder that already holds a catalogue`, `Export my library writes every user entry, inactive ones included, and no built-in`, `an export with nothing to write is refused` over both stores, `a catalogue export pins the version row of every exported kind`, `a catalogue export target is named by its folder` and `every export error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 14; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.
